{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## CORRECTION to my own RCA: this failure is NOT always fatal to a review. Severity refined, mechanism unchanged.\n\nA sibling session ([rebar:aec1-76e7-bb95-4c86], via the usage instrumentation it just landed) produced evidence that **falsifies part of my framing**, and it is right.\n\n### What it measured\n\nFour recorded gate calls, all `plan-review-prerequisite-verifier`, all `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6`, at **185.6-185.7s with `requests=0`** (no model request ever completed — a pre-response 400). That is an exact match for the grammar-compilation fingerprint established here, independently recorded, and it is a tighter fingerprint than mine because `requests=0` proves nothing was generated.\n\n**And then this:** the attestation for aec1 signed at **19:03:13 UTC** while that step failed at **19:03:10 — three seconds earlier, inside the run that PASSED and CERTIFIED.** The workaround was NOT set; the model was stock sonnet-4-6; no `--force`. Across three runs the timeout was CONSTANT while the verdict moved (indeterminate findings 14 -> 3 -> 0, INDETERMINATE -> INDETERMINATE -> PASS). A constant cannot explain a variable.\n\n### What I got wrong\n\nMy RCA said the failure means \"the review lands INDETERMINATE and unsigned\" and that a ticket in this state \"cannot be claimed\". **That overstates it.** The correct statement:\n\n* The failing step is specifically `prerequisite_verify` — the PREREQUISITE-consistency verifier — **not** the main Pass-2 `verify` step. Only prerequisite findings depend on it.\n* Whether the review still signs therefore depends on whether that run produced prerequisite findings that mattered. When it did (c827's two runs, aec1 rounds 3-4) the verdict degraded to INDETERMINATE. When it did not, the review signed anyway — demonstrated.\n* So the original reporter's observation and the sibling's PASS are BOTH true; they are different runs, not a contradiction.\n\nThis also retires the last of my \"finding count\" framing: the discriminator was never plan size, it is whether the degraded prerequisite findings were load-bearing for that verdict.\n\n### What this does NOT change\n\nThe mechanism is unchanged and still proven: the 18ae exact-model row routes NativeOutput, Bedrock cannot compile the contract's grammar, HTTP 400. The three-way live experiment (native-tiny OK 2.0s / native-big FAIL 185.3s / prompted-big OK 11.2s) stands, as does the blast radius (`code_review_verification`, 36 optionals, FAILS at 185.4s and is pinned `model: standard`).\n\n### Why it is still worth fixing at priority\n\nSeverity is lower than \"gate outage\" but the defect is real and, in one respect, WORSE than a loud failure:\n\n1. **Every affected review burns ~185s of wall clock** producing nothing — pure waste on both gates, on every run, silently.\n2. **Prerequisite consistency is never actually verified on this model.** The step cannot return a verdict, so those findings are unverifiable by construction. A review can sign while that check was never performed. A gate that appears to run a check it structurally cannot complete is a correctness hole, not just a slow path.\n3. It is a REGRESSION with a known introducing commit, and the fix is small and scoped.\n\n### Note for whoever picks this up\n\nThe sibling also reports a **distinct** failure mode that must NOT be folded into this ticket: `overlap-judge` failing at **312-381s with `requests=3`** — real requests completed, different duration band, different cause. Separate root cause; file separately.\n\nCaveat on the corroborating data: 4 samples, one step, one host, and the sibling did not capture the Bedrock 400 body. It corroborates the fingerprint; the schema-complexity mechanism proven above remains the mechanism of record."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785958259824387001,"uuid":"1b6cdc1c-5600-48a6-a65d-d3c6a4877a56"}